    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d273">

                <pb facs="0334" n="218" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg218"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.51/1266.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Sullivan.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-03-20T12:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 20, 1914, 12 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cable immediately if there appears to be any apparent evidence on the part of
                    Congress to change its position as to authorization of loan or if its position
                    could be changed in reference to authorization of means for the payment of back
                    salaries only. The payment of back salaries might be arrived at by a temporary
                    advance of $500,000 <pb facs="0335" n="219" xml:id="pg219"/> from public works
                    funds on deposit in New York if Congress would authorize the pledging of alcohol
                    and stamp taxes to repay this loan. If this is not possible request Minister of
                    Finance to prepare plan for efficacious repayment.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
